{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104850","id":2429329697,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6QzKEh","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104850","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104850.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104850.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104850","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104850/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104850/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104850/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/207a2b64723f8944a02897af3c2fcced5e3ed964","number":104850,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Core: Integrate warning suppression macro helpers","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"While looking into potential PRs for tackling ignored errors in a more methodical manner, I've realized just how invasive a lot of these suppression fields really are. Inspired by similar wrappers from some of our thirdparty libraries, this PR integrates new macros to streamline and consolidate the warning suppression process.\r\n\r\nBefore:\r\n```cpp\r\n#if defined(__GNUC__) && !defined(__clang__)\r\n#pragma GCC diagnostic push\r\n#pragma GCC diagnostic ignored \"-Wsome-warning\"\r\n#endif\r\n...\r\n#if defined(__GNUC__) && !defined(__clang__)\r\n#pragma GCC diagnostic pop\r\n#endif\r\n```\r\nAfter:\r\n```cpp\r\nGODOT_GCC_WARNING_PUSH_AND_IGNORE(\"-Wsome-warning\")\r\n...\r\nGODOT_GCC_WARNING_POP\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe name is a bit verbose, but that's the intent; this isn't something we want misused. To ensure no clashes, and to abide by the standard forbidding leading underscores, `GODOT` was chosen as the prefix for all of these macros. The next section is the compiler, in this case one of `GCC`, `CLANG`, or `MSVC`. Following that is the primary action, which has two instances: `PRAGMA` and `WARNING`. `WARNING` has subcategories for the common suppression calls: `PUSH`, `IGNORE`, and `POP`. There's one hybrid subcategory, `PUSH_AND_IGNORE`, for the instances with only a single warning to allow for one-liners.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":283518733,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODM1MTg3MzM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/usability","name":"usability","description":"","color":"447744","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2304948121,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMzA0OTQ4M